@startuml heart-mcp-act
title One act through heart-mcp: water bed 2 with 250 ml
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
autonumber

participant "Model\n(in Claude Code)" as model
participant "heart-mcp" as mcp
participant "ARTIE" as artie
participant "Garden server" as garden
database "Postgres" as db

== Look first ==
model -> mcp : heart_look(service: "garden"), then heart_follow to bed 2
mcp -> artie : enter bookmark, follow link
artie -> garden : GET bed 2 (HAL), GET its forms
garden --> artie : state + ETag, offered acts + schemas
artie -> artie : hold representation and ETag
mcp --> model : state, acts (water-cell + schema), links\nno URLs, no ETag

== Act ==
model -> mcp : heart_act(act: "garden:water-cell",\nfields: {milliliters: 250})
mcp -> mcp : check held copy:\nact offered? fields fit schema?
alt act not offered, or fields break the schema
  mcp --> model : rejected-before-sending\n(nothing sent)
else checks pass
  mcp -> artie : act
  artie -> garden : POST water-cell\nIf-Match: ETag the model saw
  alt 200
    garden -> db : append WaterApplied row
    garden --> artie : new state, new acts
    mcp --> model : acted\n(water no longer offered)
  else 412 someone changed the bed first
    garden --> artie : precondition failed
    artie -> garden : GET bed again
    mcp --> model : stale, fresh state\n(act never resent)
  else 409 act no longer legal
    artie -> garden : GET bed again
    mcp --> model : not-offered, fresh state
  else 422 rule-refused
    garden --> artie : "at most 600 ml now"
    mcp --> model : rule-refused, in the bed's words
  else 422 invalid input
    mcp --> model : invalid-input, with violations
  end
end

note over model, artie
  The model only chooses.
  heart-mcp checks the choice. ARTIE builds every request.
end note
@enduml
